title: Real-Time Clock
files:
  - em.core:em.hal/RtcI.em.ts
  - em.core:em.utils/TimeTypes.em.ts
  - em.core:em.utils/AlarmMgr.em.ts
  - em.core:em.utils/UptimerRtc.em.ts
  - .assets/img-101-08-01.png

steps:

  - cmds:
      - view 5
    text: |

      {[ht,$start] Real-Time Clock}

      The {[cu]AlarmMgr} implementation covered in this tour lev&shy;erages a {[cs]$proxy} conforming to the {[cu]RtcI} interface.

      We'll initially visit {[cu]RtcI} before pivoting to {[cu]TimerTypes} definitions &ndash; used throughout this design.

      After exploring {[cu]AlarmMgr}, we'll visit {[cu]UptimerRtc} &ndash; a bridge between the {[cu]UptimerI} and {[cu]RtcI} abstractions.

  - cmds:
      - open 1
    focus: [1,1]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |

      {[ht,$peek] %[cu]RtcI% &ndash; Quick Look }

      The {[cu]RtcI} interface exposes methods reflecting differ&shy;ent aspects of MCU real-time clock [RTC] peripherals:

      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} {[cf]enable}&middot;{[cf]disable} capture timer-like RTC behavior<br>
      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} {[cf]getRawTime} captures clock-like RTC behavior<br>
      {[bi,arrow_circle_right]} {[cf]toThresh} maps to an internal RTC timebase

      All of these methods rely upon a set of _time types_ defined in our conventionally-named module {[cu]T}.

      {[in]Unlike other <code>em.hal</code> interfaces we've seen, %[cu]RtcI% im&shy;plementations can vary considerably between MCUs.}

  - cmds:
      - open 2
      - mark 2 A 11
      - mark 2 B 24
      - mark 2 C 28
    focus: [2,1]
    acts: [$reveal]
    text: |

      {[ht,$details] %[cu]TimeTypes% &ndash; Details }

      You've already seen many of these types and functions used by {[cu]RtcI} as well as by clients of {[cu]AlarmMgr}.

      <div class="em-bmlist">
      
      {[bm,A]} {[ct]RawTime} represents the current time since reset as the fixed-point value {[cn]secs}.{[cn]subs} in Q32.32 format.

      {[bm,B]} These three 32-bit types represent different _time deltas_ &ndash; each with their own range and precision.

      {[bm,C]} A set of helper functions for converting between time types and for obtaining a type's zero value.

      </div>

      {[in]The <i>accuracy</i> of these time values depends upon the underlying RTC &ndash; quite different with every MCU.}

